Python (ryoku/shell/quickshell/shell/modules/bar/barstyles/python/)

Python is a Ryoku bar style based on Serpantinum, created by ilyamiro and
contributors (https://github.com/ilyamiro/serpantinum). It is a modified
version: the QML surfaces are ported near-verbatim, while the data plane runs
through Ryoku's window-manager seam, settings daemon, palette and services.

This port tracks Serpantinum at commit 3619689, release 2.3.1. It includes the
upstream bars, faces, media surfaces, guide and standalone settings window,
launcher, clipboard presentation, policy prompt presentation, quick actions,
wellbeing views and widget-face library. Ryoku supplies the application
catalogue, clipboard history, policy agent, recorder, notifications, wallpaper,
window-manager state, configuration storage, dock host and widget host.

The port intentionally leaves out Ski and its file picker and pins, the lock
editor, fingerprint and PAM code, Serpantinum's screenshot and OCR stack,
Tesseract integration, installers and AUR or Nix packaging, telemetry, updater
and first-run flow. Wallpaper, capture, qylock, idle, updates, Super+Escape,
desktop widgets and the universal dock remain Ryoku surfaces.

